# Question: how much value do we lose if a feature ships later than planned,
# and how likely is the delay to cost more than 100k euros?
#
# Run it (it uses the shared formulas):
#   ubc --scenario product/cost-of-delay
# Change an assumption, for example a delay of two to four weeks:
#   ubc --set 'delay_weeks = 2 to 4' --scenario product/cost-of-delay
# See which assumption matters most:
#   ubc --sens cost --scenario product/cost-of-delay
#
# Every "a to b" is a 90% confidence interval. Amounts are in euros. Cost of
# delay (Don Reinertsen): the value a feature brings every week it is in
# users' hands is lost for every week it is not.

# Assumptions
customers = 200 to 600            # customers who would use the feature; ask sales or look at the requests
value_per_customer = 20 to 60     # extra revenue or savings a week for each of them
delay_weeks = 4 to 12             # how much later than planned it ships

# Calculation
weekly_value = customers * value_per_customer      # the cost of delay: value lost every week
cost = delay_cost(weekly_value, delay_weeks)       # value lost over the whole delay

# Result
weekly_value
cost
P(cost > 100k)                    # how likely is the delay to cost more than 100k euros?
